it is being called a game changer and  the start of a new era germany  has promised to begin returning the  artifacts known as the benin bronzes  to nigeria next year making it the first  country to do so  germany has a collection of just over 1  000 benin bronzers they're on display in  museums in cologne in dresden  hamburg leipzig and stuttgart now the  sculptures and metal plaques  are from the ancient kingdom of bernin  which is today known as  edor state in southern nigeria the  bronzes were looted by british soldiers  in 1897 and sold to museums in north  america and europe  the largest collection of the bronzes is  held by the british  museum nigeria has been trying to get  back the bronzes for  decades without success but momentum has  been building over the last few years  with  cores growing ever louder for artifacts  seized during the  colonial era to be returned to their  places of origin  germany's culture minister explained why  berlin had decided to act now she said  quote we are confronting our historic  and moral responsibility  we want to contribute to a common  understanding  and reconciliation with the descendants  of the people  who were robbed of their cultural  treasures during the time  of colonialism close quote  the benin bronzes some of africa's most  prized treasures for decades demands for  their restitution have grown louder  now cultural and political leaders have  agreed to begin  returning the artifacts held in german  museums  by next year  i must admit i cannot believe it but  there was a posit very positive result  and everybody was  agreed to it that the being albanian  bronzes the banin  looted art has to go back to nigeria  so this is this is really great  really great news and a significant  change of heart the bronzes were due to  be showcased at berlin's new  humboldt forum just a few weeks ago the  foundation which currently holds the  bronzes  was reticent about the possibility of  returning  they can be seen in them muse