elf  we know that many of the heads  are heads of kings of beni  so the narrative being told  if you take that with you if you loot it  if you plunder it  it means you are taking the memory of a  particular kingdom  so this is why it is not just the moral  aspect  it is really a way of reconnecting a  memory that has been fragmented it is a  remembering  of the african memory and that is  professor suleiman bashir  diana thank you professor it's been  great having your views on this topic  thank you for having me  we sent our team uh out to get some  reaction from people in nigeria where  the news has been welcomed but  but as you're about to hear there are  some doubts  too do we trust ourselves  some people will surely go there and  loot it and sell it send it back to the  another country that need it  i think the problem is every one of us  not only the government  do we trust ourselves  if we the german are returning it i  think we should ease our assets we  should keep it  i believe they should even return it  back to the very uh edu states  and they should now android i think  there should be a museum there  owned by the federal government and the  people is the assets  so they will take care of it very well  but if you leave it somewhere in lagos  or abuja anybody can go in there and  loot it  and that's the end we're back to square  one  i mean um nigeria being we  we we are we may not be able  because we don't appreciate all those  things but at the same time  is our own then it should be returned  back  to this country and uh we should uh  every individual every state should do  i mean one of the things to keep those  scenes  they they are very important to us they  are more or less like a foundation  to we should keep it our own job needs  to return our hard work  back to nigeria but the issue we have in  nigeria is  security how we can how the government  will be able to protect these  artworks when they are finally resolved  but it's our asset in nigeri